Here $k=3>0$, so the parabola is concave up with a minimum turning point.

Since $c=-12$, the vertex and $y$-intercept are $(0,-12)$. The minimum value is $-12$ and the axis of symmetry is $x=0$.

For the $x$-intercepts, let $y=0$:
$\begin{aligned}0&=3x^2-12\\3x^2&=12\\x^2&=4\\x&=\pm2\end{aligned}$

The $x$-intercepts are $(-2,0)$ and $(2,0)$.

Plot these points and draw a smooth parabola symmetric about $x=0$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=2mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[<->,black] (-3.2,0)--(3.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-15)--(0,9) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[dashed,black] (0,-14)--(0,8);
\draw[curveblue,thick,<->,domain=-2.5:2.5,samples=80,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{3*(\x)*(\x)-12});
\fill[black] (-2,0) circle (1.5pt);
\fill[black] (2,0) circle (1.5pt);
\fill[black] (0,-12) circle (1.5pt);
\path (-2,0) node[above left] {$(-2,0)$};
\path (2,0) node[above right] {$(2,0)$};
\path (0,-12) node[below right] {$(0,-12)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

